WEBVTT

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:13.670
The youthful, embracing sea, decorated with waves...

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:24.120
The water's edge hides the peaceful corpses of the dead.

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:32.290
The meld of souls that fashions itself into a Koromo...

00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:41.430
triggers the whistling of the winter winds.

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:47.050
Chapter Three

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:47.050
Asuka

00:04:59.080 --> 00:04:59.960
Look here.

00:05:01.710 --> 00:05:03.210
So frigid.

00:05:03.210 --> 00:05:05.380
You've changed your tune since you agreed to this.

00:05:05.380 --> 00:05:06.710
That's not true.

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:12.720
C'mon, let's chat.

00:05:13.260 --> 00:05:15.510
Chat? About what?

00:05:15.510 --> 00:05:18.560
What we were talking about earlier – the Red Army hunting people.

00:05:19.270 --> 00:05:21.520
I've already told you all I know.

00:05:22.060 --> 00:05:25.860
It's not like I've seen it happen. I don't know the details.

00:05:26.570 --> 00:05:28.070
You really don't know anything else?

00:05:30.070 --> 00:05:32.070
Have you heard those rumors about vampires?

00:05:32.360 --> 00:05:35.030
Vampires? Like Count Dracula?

00:05:35.030 --> 00:05:37.240
Yeah, something like that.

00:05:37.240 --> 00:05:39.910
I've heard there have been some prowling around the city lately.

00:05:40.410 --> 00:05:42.750
You reckon the Great Disaster caused that too?

00:05:42.750 --> 00:05:44.080
I'm guessing so.

00:05:44.500 --> 00:05:47.090
I hear they've got pointy fangs as well.

00:05:47.500 --> 00:05:51.590
They find hot chicks and jump them like this!

00:05:53.090 --> 00:05:55.050
That's gonna take you into overtime rates.

00:05:58.390 --> 00:05:59.600
Come again soon.

00:06:00.770 --> 00:06:02.600
Did you get anything useful, Rai?

00:06:03.350 --> 00:06:06.570
Nothing solid. Just rumors.

00:06:08.980 --> 00:06:11.820
What's all this about vampires anyway? Makes me laugh.

00:06:11.820 --> 00:06:14.990
Why don't you stop whoring yourself out then?

00:06:15.990 --> 00:06:20.080
I'm not suited to getting information the respectable way.

00:06:20.370 --> 00:06:24.040
What about you? Have you found anyone who's good in a fight yet?

00:06:24.040 --> 00:06:28.590
Not yet. I've worn my shoes down to their soles looking, and some nasty characters have started watching me.

00:06:28.960 --> 00:06:30.550
You poor bastard.

00:06:30.550 --> 00:06:32.510
That means I win our little bet.

00:06:32.510 --> 00:06:35.640
Hold on there. I've still got time.

00:06:36.390 --> 00:06:38.390
You want to sleep with me that badly?

00:06:38.970 --> 00:06:39.810
Guess so.

00:06:42.930 --> 00:06:44.230
Where are you off to?

00:06:44.900 --> 00:06:46.150
Looking for customers.

00:06:46.150 --> 00:06:47.810
Meet me at Sakafune at nine, okay?

00:06:47.810 --> 00:06:49.190
I'll be waiting.

00:06:51.940 --> 00:06:55.910
I say that, but I still have no clue where to start, huh?

00:07:25.810 --> 00:07:28.310
Hey, Bro, you looking for some fun?

00:07:29.690 --> 00:07:31.190
What name does this metropolis go by?

00:07:31.190 --> 00:07:31.980
What?

00:07:32.190 --> 00:07:33.860
What name do you give to this country?

00:07:34.360 --> 00:07:35.110
Come again?

00:07:39.280 --> 00:07:41.370
That guy ain't right in the head.

00:07:58.180 --> 00:08:00.430
Hey there, what are you doing up there?

00:08:03.720 --> 00:08:04.980
What is this place?

00:08:04.980 --> 00:08:06.140
Huh?

00:08:06.140 --> 00:08:07.850
This is Asuka.

00:08:08.560 --> 00:08:09.730
Asuka...

00:08:09.730 --> 00:08:10.900
Yamato?

00:08:12.360 --> 00:08:14.400
That weapon of his looks dangerous.

00:08:15.490 --> 00:08:17.190
H-Hey now!

00:08:17.570 --> 00:08:18.490
Wait a second!

00:08:20.280 --> 00:08:21.370
Excuse me.

00:08:21.370 --> 00:08:23.620
Where are you from?

00:08:24.790 --> 00:08:25.950
Are you looking for someone?

00:08:28.040 --> 00:08:28.960
My sword.

00:08:29.670 --> 00:08:32.630
That kid just fleeced you.

00:08:32.630 --> 00:08:36.010
You're best off forgetting about it. You won't see it again.

00:08:41.510 --> 00:08:44.220
Hey old man, I've got a question for you.

00:08:44.220 --> 00:08:46.020
Oh, Mr. Karuta.

00:08:46.350 --> 00:08:48.730
Are there any trades going on in these parts?

00:08:48.730 --> 00:08:50.520
Yeah, there are.

00:08:50.520 --> 00:08:53.440
Today and tomorrow, there's one in Ashikari.

00:08:53.440 --> 00:08:55.030
Are the Yukigumi organizing it?

00:08:55.030 --> 00:08:56.650
No, the Kazegumi.

00:08:56.650 --> 00:08:59.530
Really? Thanks very much.

00:09:01.410 --> 00:09:03.160
Oh, Mr. Karuta!

00:09:03.160 --> 00:09:06.370
Hi, Miss Izumi. As always, you look great today.

00:09:06.620 --> 00:09:09.370
What's the rush, Karuta? You playing around again?

00:09:09.660 --> 00:09:11.540
Just on a job.

00:09:25.930 --> 00:09:27.430
Roll up!

00:09:34.650 --> 00:09:35.980
Give it here.

00:09:38.030 --> 00:09:39.110
Looks cheap.

00:09:40.030 --> 00:09:41.900
There it is–

00:09:42.110 --> 00:09:43.820
Hey, what do you want?!

00:09:43.820 --> 00:09:45.990
What are you doing?!

00:09:47.280 --> 00:09:48.120
You got some nerve!

00:09:48.120 --> 00:09:48.830
You cocksucker!

00:09:50.210 --> 00:09:51.410
You're asking for it...

00:09:51.920 --> 00:09:54.000
Wait! Wait!

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:55.210
Mr. Karuta!

00:09:55.590 --> 00:09:57.630
I'll take care of this.

00:09:57.630 --> 00:09:59.800
Let me buy this sword off you.

00:09:59.800 --> 00:10:04.430
If that's how it is, please just take it for free.

00:10:04.430 --> 00:10:06.470
Oh, really? Such kindness.

00:10:07.060 --> 00:10:08.890
Come on, let's go.

00:10:17.270 --> 00:10:18.400
I proffer my apologies to you.

00:10:18.400 --> 00:10:20.030
What for?

00:10:20.030 --> 00:10:21.860
This is mine now.

00:10:23.650 --> 00:10:26.070
If you want it back, you'd better follow me.

00:10:26.070 --> 00:10:27.950
I'm heading for a shop called Sakafune.

00:10:46.710 --> 00:10:48.710
So, Kuro, where are you from?

00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:53.640
Even after boozing, you don't speak much.

00:10:56.720 --> 00:10:57.550
Over there...

00:10:57.550 --> 00:11:01.190
Huh? That's a painting by Tonba.

00:11:01.430 --> 00:11:03.680
He's one of our bosses.

00:11:03.680 --> 00:11:05.140
He's always sketching.

00:11:05.770 --> 00:11:08.150
That's a scene from the Great Disaster.

00:11:08.150 --> 00:11:09.870
The Great Disaster?

00:11:11.820 --> 00:11:14.040
When the stars fell to Earth for seven days straight.

00:11:19.990 --> 00:11:22.050
Why don't I just start from the beginning?

00:11:22.910 --> 00:11:26.960
Twenty-four years ago, there was an asteroid heading towards the Earth.

00:11:28.540 --> 00:11:33.000
Every country sent their nukes up to destroy it, but...

00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:34.670
they didn't make it in time.

00:11:35.630 --> 00:11:41.940
During the chaos, some countries also fired missiles at other countries instead of the asteroid.

00:11:43.010 --> 00:11:46.140
Nation after nation fell under the attack,

00:11:46.140 --> 00:11:50.610
leading to the destruction of all the world powers.

00:11:52.690 --> 00:11:57.150
Even so, up until that point, a seventh of the world's population had survived.

00:11:58.860 --> 00:12:01.070
But what came next for these survivors,

00:12:01.070 --> 00:12:03.490
and for every living creature on the planet...

00:12:03.490 --> 00:12:08.470
Well, it was another eye-opener.

00:12:09.250 --> 00:12:12.420
It was a nuclear winter.

00:12:14.130 --> 00:12:16.630
The nuclear winter lasted for over a year.

00:12:17.630 --> 00:12:24.810
It took two and a half years for a weak sun to bring us daylight again.

00:12:26.180 --> 00:12:32.120
During this period, the populace of Japan reduced to a sliver of what it had once been.

00:12:32.560 --> 00:12:35.650
By that time, television and radio transmissions had ceased,

00:12:36.690 --> 00:12:39.620
so how could anyone be aware of the full extent of the world's plight?

00:12:40.580 --> 00:12:44.630
No human, without substantial exertion, should have been able to acquire such knowledge.

00:12:47.120 --> 00:12:48.880
Do you not agree?

00:12:49.580 --> 00:12:51.890
What say you, Kuro?

00:14:32.980 --> 00:14:35.150
You're telling me it was the Red Emperor?!

00:14:35.850 --> 00:14:36.820
Yes.

00:14:36.820 --> 00:14:38.060
What does this mean?

00:14:38.540 --> 00:14:39.700
Why have they come here?!

00:14:41.400 --> 00:14:43.700
I'm guessing it's to do with their people hunting.

00:14:45.450 --> 00:14:47.040
I'm heading over there now.

00:14:47.040 --> 00:14:48.490
Take the weapons to Sakafune–

00:15:00.040 --> 00:15:02.060
Rai! Rai!

00:15:05.430 --> 00:15:07.270
Get those lights turned off this instant!

00:15:07.570 --> 00:15:09.100
Go to the painting.

00:15:09.100 --> 00:15:10.760
Go and hide behind the painting.

00:15:10.760 --> 00:15:11.730
You don't mean...

00:15:12.180 --> 00:15:14.650
Yes. It's the Red Army.

00:15:26.200 --> 00:15:26.950
Take this.

00:15:26.950 --> 00:15:27.820
Thanks.

00:15:34.160 --> 00:15:35.760
Karuta, can you hear me?

00:15:35.760 --> 00:15:37.830
Rai, are you all right?

00:15:37.830 --> 00:15:39.760
The Red Army's helicopters are heading your way.

00:15:40.250 --> 00:15:41.380
How many are we facing?

00:15:41.380 --> 00:15:41.890
Give me a second.

00:15:50.350 --> 00:15:52.270
There's a six man scout team coming towards you.

00:15:52.640 --> 00:15:55.150
They're about fifteen meters from the entrance.

00:15:55.810 --> 00:15:57.940
You've got thirty seconds!

00:15:57.940 --> 00:15:59.070
Got it.

00:15:59.070 --> 00:16:01.580
Come now, you too.

00:17:46.130 --> 00:17:47.060
Kuro!

00:18:22.790 --> 00:18:25.260
That was a close one.

00:18:25.260 --> 00:18:29.000
Still, you've got some muscle there.

00:19:04.790 --> 00:19:09.710
If there comes a time when you have convalesced from your wounds, we shall meet again.

00:19:34.940 --> 00:19:35.950
What's he up to?

00:20:13.180 --> 00:20:28.170
Next Chapter

00:20:18.330 --> 00:20:28.170
The Haniwa
